        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Respondent&#8217;s transportation and storage services bundled under its TSS Rate Schedule are reported separately in this filing pursuant to the limited waiver granted in Docket No. AC08-120-000.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Respondent&#8217;s transportation and storage services bundled under its TSS Rate Schedule are reported separately in this filing pursuant to the limited waiver granted in Docket No. AC08-120-000.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Respondent&#8217;s transportation and storage services bundled under its TSS Rate Schedule are reported separately in this filing pursuant to the limited waiver granted in Docket No. AC08-120-000.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amount shown represents the difference between physical withdrawals and contractual withdrawals.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amount shown represents Gas Received from Shippers as Compressor Fuel and an allocation of the previous year&#8217;s over/under collection surcharge percentage. Respondent does not segregate transportation surcharge percentages between fuel and loss.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amount shown represents Gas Received from Shippers as Lost and Unaccounted For and an allocation of the previous year&#8217;s over/under collection surcharge percentage. Respondent does not segregate surcharge percentages between fuel and loss.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Other Receipts include Operational Balancing Agreements (OBAs), suspense, and receipt of Respondent&#8217;s production gas.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">For the purpose of the ACA calculation, the throughput volume is represented on line 20.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amount shown represents the difference between physical injections and contractual injections.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Other Deliveries include OBAs, suspense, right-of-way obligations, company used fuel, compressor station fuel, gas drained, any differences between physical and contractual deliveries, and third-party storage as defined in Respondent&#8217;s FERC Gas Tariff &#8211; Section 29.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The allocation of Dth reported in column (e) to the appropriate contract type is based on the percentage of the Respondent&#8217;s firm contracts with a discount rate, a negotiated rate, or a recourse rate.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The allocation of Dth reported in column (e) to the appropriate contract type is based on the percentage of the Respondent&#8217;s firm contracts with a discount rate, a negotiated rate, or a recourse rate.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The allocation of Dth reported in column (e) to the appropriate contract type is based on the percentage of the Respondent&#8217;s firm contracts with a discount rate, a negotiated rate, or a recourse rate.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The basis in valuing the gas reported in column (f) is based on the current month spot price published in Platts Gas Daily Price Guide.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The basis in valuing the gas reported in column (f) is based on the current month spot price published in Platts Gas Daily Price Guide.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The basis in valuing the gas reported in column (f) is based on the current month spot price published in Platts Gas Daily Price Guide.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Respondent uses a fuel and loss tracker whereby over/under recovery of volumes from shippers accumulates for the fuel and loss filing period; therefore, Respondent does not buy or sell fuel and loss gas. Volumes due to or from shippers as a result of over or under recovery of actual fuel and loss are recorded on the Comparative Balance Sheets in FERC Accounts 182.3 and 242 (under recovery) or FERC Accounts 174 and 254 (over recovery). Cumulative over/under recovery balances are revalued each month using current month spot price published in Platts Gas Daily Price Guide.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Respondent uses a fuel and loss tracker whereby over/under recovery of volumes from shippers accumulates for the fuel and loss filing period; therefore, Respondent does not buy or sell fuel and loss gas. Volumes due to or from shippers as a result of over or under recovery of actual fuel and loss are recorded on the Comparative Balance Sheets in FERC Accounts 182.3 and 242 (under recovery) or FERC Accounts 174 and 254 (over recovery). Cumulative over/under recovery balances are revalued each month using current month spot price published in Platts Gas Daily Price Guide.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Respondent uses a fuel and loss tracker whereby over/under recovery of volumes from shippers accumulates for the fuel and loss filing period; therefore, Respondent does not buy or sell fuel and loss gas. Volumes due to or from shippers as a result of over or under recovery of actual fuel and loss are recorded on the Comparative Balance Sheets in FERC Accounts 182.3 and 242 (under recovery) or FERC Accounts 174 and 254 (over recovery). Cumulative over/under recovery balances are revalued each month using current month spot price published in Platts Gas Daily Price Guide.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The sum of the volumes in columns (e) on line 22 is 200,903 Dth which includes other company used fuel, gas drained and right-of-way obligations. The total from page 521 of 200,903 Dth compares to the amount of (3,990,249) Dth listed on line 29, column (d), on Page 520. The (3,990,249) Dth on Page 520 includes OBA, suspense, right-of-way obligations, company used fuel, gas drained, any differences between physical and contractual deliveries, and third-party storage as defined in Respondent&#8217;s FERC Gas Tariff- Section 29. The difference of 4,191,152 Dth is related to OBAs, suspense, any differences between physical and contractual deliveries and third-party storage as defined in Respondent&#8217;s FERC Gas Tariff- Section 29.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Under recovery of volumes from shippers compared to the actual fuel and loss experienced on a cumulative basis for the current fuel tracker cycle.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Under recovery of volumes from shippers compared to the actual fuel and loss experienced on a cumulative basis for the current fuel tracker cycle.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Over recovery of volumes from shippers compared to the actual fuel and loss experienced on a cumulative basis for the current fuel tracker cycle.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
